{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish","id":607021,"title":"Changeling: the Dreaming 20 wish","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-29T13:43:06-07:00","id":607021,"title":"Changeling: the Dreaming 20 wish","content":"If I could have one wish for the hypothetical C:tD 20, it would be that the canon Kiths at best constitute a minority of the Kiths still surviving on earth. Maybe they are the largest minorities, because they were better organized and connected, but still just a minority.<br /> <br /> Edit: In Dreams and Nightmares, it mentioned how there were a pair of Chimera who were either once True Fae or had the ability to become True Fae. I wouldn't mind if the book mentions how every now and then a Chimera successfully becomes a True Fae and emerges from the Dreaming to becom a Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-29-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:56:15-07:00","id":607156,"title":"","content":"Bygone Bestiary has rules for creating chimera as beasts. Just add the Willpower, Banality and Glamour ratings for the appropriate seeming, make sure they have the equivalent of two birthrights and one frailty (the birthrights can be bought as special advantages, but the frailty can come from a flaw which they don't get extra Freebies for), and you have a custom changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:53:30-07:00","id":607197,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an awfully big of a departure for a 20th anniversary edition. But if it follows Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, there should be lots of options. In addition to the nine core kiths, there are the minor kiths, the Nunnehi kiths, the Menehune kiths, Inanimae kiths, Hsien kiths, Adhene kiths, and Thallain kiths. If even part of those are in there, folks shouldn't be hurting for options.<br /> <br /> As for chimera becoming true fae, that was the way it worked before the shattering according to DA: Fae. The world is too calcified by banality for it happen these days, but there's nothing stopping you from doing something with that in your game. In fact, that could be a great seed for a chronicle - a chimera has grown powerful and fundamental enough to the Dreaming it's on the verge of becoming a true fae. Banality is keeping it from realizing it's full potential, and it's up to the PCs to help it cross that line. If they succeed, the Dreaming gets a huge boost as the first new kith is born since the Shattering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:25:42-07:00","id":607238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607197#post607197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an awfully big of a departure for a 20th anniversary edition. But if it follows Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, there should be lots of options. In addition to the nine core kiths, there are the minor kiths, the Nunnehi kiths, the Menehune kiths, Inanimae kiths, Hsien kiths, Adhene kiths, and Thallain kiths. If even part of those are in there, folks shouldn't be hurting for options.<br /> <br /> As for chimera becoming true fae, that was the way it worked before the shattering according to DA: Fae. The world is too calcified by banality for it happen these days, but there's nothing stopping you from doing something with that in your game. In fact, that could be a great seed for a chronicle - a chimera has grown powerful and fundamental enough to the Dreaming it's on the verge of becoming a true fae. Banality is keeping it from realizing it's full potential, and it's up to the PCs to help it cross that line. If they succeed, the Dreaming gets a huge boost as the first new kith is born since the Shattering.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some nice fan rules for customising existing kiths, as well. I like the idea of picking your main kith, and then adding on the special bonuses/flaws of the CTL sub-kiths. So you could have a troll who's also a beast/skitterskulk. It stacks a lot of unique modifiers and special abilities, but the difference between two characters of the same kith would be vast. It's not necessarily something I'd put in the core book, but perhaps an option to buy Redes as PC Merits so as to customise kiths would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:30:56-07:00","id":607251,"title":"","content":"Rules for True Fae, even if they're poorly suited to handle Banality.<br /> <br /> A set of rules for constructing your own fae. It is better than create a lot of kiths, to simply state that other kiths can exist and them make a rule for kith-creation. Changeling: The Lost already have some descent matherial in that regard. It can be adapted and even improved.<br /> <br /> By all the gods, a clearer explanation about Glamour and Banality, so you can best define them.<br /> <br /> Crossover rules. And no rules that realy only discourages implementing something, like making vampires so harmful to Fae that it is almost impossible for them to cooperate on a mixed group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T18:23:53-07:00","id":607326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607197#post607197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an awfully big of a departure for a 20th anniversary edition. But if it follows Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, there should be lots of options. In addition to the nine core kiths, there are the minor kiths, the Nunnehi kiths, the Menehune kiths, Inanimae kiths, Hsien kiths, Adhene kiths, and Thallain kiths. If even part of those are in there, folks shouldn't be hurting for options.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Thallain are basically just Fae BSDs or Baali, but I hear what you are saying. Still, they fail by themselves as just the dreams of (mostly) Europeans. If they were the minority in Concordia it would be more believable than how things stand now. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607197#post607197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for chimera becoming true fae, that was the way it worked before the shattering according to DA: Fae. The world is too calcified by banality for it happen these days, but there's nothing stopping you from doing something with that in your game. In fact, that could be a great seed for a chronicle - a chimera has grown powerful and fundamental enough to the Dreaming it's on the verge of becoming a true fae. Banality is keeping it from realizing it's full potential, and it's up to the PCs to help it cross that line. If they succeed, the Dreaming gets a huge boost as the first new kith is born since the Shattering.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we're not talking about meat space, just the Deep Dreaming. It seems reasonable that it could happen if only rarely, and under certain circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T23:58:01-07:00","id":607532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607326#post607326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Thallain are basically just Fae BSDs or Baali, but I hear what you are saying. Still, they fail by themselves as just the dreams of (mostly) Europeans. If they were the minority in Concordia it would be more believable than how things stand now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given European dominance of North America, why is it difficult to believe that the Kithain would be the majority there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T01:30:24-07:00","id":607555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607532#post607532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given European dominance of North America, why is it difficult to believe that the Kithain would be the majority there?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. What's difficult is the notion that their dreams would be so limited. The Kithain's diversity should be more like Changeling: the Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-30-2015, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:50:10-07:00","id":608052,"title":"","content":"Since they're doing the hsien, I'm going to hope that, depending on what they keep, the Chu-ih-yu get their name changed to something that's actually recognizable in Romanized form. Looking at it, and keeping in mind the track record for how some Wade-Giles... mutated when used by WW*, to say the least, it seems like it's a mangled form of Ch'ih-yu, (written Chiyou in Hanyu Pinyin). Chiyou was a great opponent of Huangdi, the Yellow Emperor, and seems to have little to nothing to do with the wuxing of metal, but then, Sui-jen (Suiren in pinyin) is the name given to the water kamuii, and the legendary emperor Suiren is credited with the use of fire.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Some typos of the name for the dragon tear Discipline in The 1000 Hells are more accurate than its KotE-given transcription. The correct form in W-G is Ch'ih Mu.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-30-2015, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T11:09:36-07:00","id":608215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607326#post607326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Thallain are basically just Fae BSDs or Baali...</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the don't HAVE to be just that 'dark mirror' version who wants to eat you up, and I sincerely hope that they receive some more nuanced interpretation in <b>C20</b>. I mean, this will be BOTH our Twentieth Anniversary AND the never-seen Revised Edition...<br /> <br /> In that same line of thought, comparing what we'll see in <b>C20</b> to what <b>Vampire</b>, <b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> (oh my!) got for their Twentieth Anniversary Editions is, I think, not an apt way of looking at it. A more likely parallel is what <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> is getting. That is, a <i>substantial</i> revision and building up of core concepts to appeal to as wide an audience as possible - both newcomers and the dyed in the wool fans. I'm not saying that we should expect to see a brand new game in <b>C20</b>, but the work done so far on <b>Wr20</b> has shown that Onyx Path is willing to make changes where needed.<br /> <br /> ...Sheesh! I don't sound like that card-carrying '<b>Changeling</b>-Hater' I used to be, do I? I think that's okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T11:29:11-07:00","id":608235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=608215#post608215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the don't HAVE to be just that 'dark mirror' version who wants to eat you up, and I sincerely hope that they receive some more nuanced interpretation in <b>C20</b>. I mean, this will be BOTH our Twentieth Anniversary AND the never-seen Revised Edition...<br /> <br /> In that same line of thought, comparing what we'll see in <b>C20</b> to what <b>Vampire</b>, <b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> (oh my!) got for their Twentieth Anniversary Editions is, I think, not an apt way of looking at it. A more likely parallel is what <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> is getting. That is, a <i>substantial</i> revision and building up of core concepts to appeal to as wide an audience as possible - both newcomers and the dyed in the wool fans. I'm not saying that we should expect to see a brand new game in <b>C20</b>, but the work done so far on <b>Wr20</b> has shown that Onyx Path is willing to make changes where needed.<br /> <br /> ...Sheesh! I don't sound like that card-carrying '<b>Changeling</b>-Hater' I used to be, do I? I think that's okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Time can only tell if Changeling will get a book with as appropriate an abbreviation as the Book of Oblivion, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T11:34:21-07:00","id":608240,"title":"","content":"G.L.A.M.O.U.R.? Or maybe D.R.E.A.M.? I have no idea what either might stand for....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:39:27-07:00","id":608399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=607555#post607555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not. What's difficult is the notion that their dreams would be soimited. The Kithain's diversity should be more like Changeling: the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. In fact, Dreaming have all the reasons to have even greater diversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:41:20-07:00","id":608756,"title":"","content":"There are a few things I'd like to see:<br /> <br /> 1. More flexibility around the scarcity of Glamour. It's notoriously difficult to obtain in the RAW, which is fine, but maybe options for making it less scarce would be welcome too. Spending weeks to get a few points is really tough, and it encourages players to hunt down dross instead.<br /> <br /> 2. Revised Realms. Actor needs work, because you can't affect an enemy until level 5! But you can fry your best friend at level one (unless he's your gaming buddy, and then he counts as an enemy). I think there should be clarification on which level of Fae a changeling needs to affect herself (I always rule a rating of zero in a Realm indicates command only over your own person and those things you own).<br /> <br /> 3. More versatility with Arts. Every Realm should be usable with every Art. Maybe each Art needs suggestions of how it might work with different Realms. Otherwise some Realms always prove more useful than others.<br /> <br /> 4. Optional rules for enchantment and the Mists for crossovers and other supernatural critters. Some of the coma periods on the Mists chart are so unforgiving that enchantment becomes a very effective weapon. Enchant a mortal and then leave them to sleep for a few weeks without remembering a thing when they awaken. Meanwhile, you burn their house down, steal their things and kill their families (if you're feeling subtle, that is...). The downtime for enchanted humans is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> 5. Clarity on what exactly Banality is for all those who argue that Technocrats aren't banal (because clearly Technocrats work magic and create wonder, while the Dauntain clearly use powers too, so it's not just 'anti-magic').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-30-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T22:02:26-07:00","id":608922,"title":"","content":"Rules should open avenues for distinct stories, not close them. So maybe supernatural critters could be immune or, at least, resistant to the Mists. It is very, very hard to work Changelings in a mixed chronicle because of the Mists. And to reduce their Banality in general would also be good for such (even if Technocrats still have high Banality, with I am one of those people who argue that they aren't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:10:36-07:00","id":609130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=608922#post608922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules should open avenues for distinct stories, not close them. So maybe supernatural critters could be immune or, at least, resistant to the Mists. It is very, very hard to work Changelings in a mixed chronicle because of the Mists. And to reduce their Banality in general would also be good for such (even if Technocrats still have high Banality, with I am one of those people who argue that they aren't).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages range from 2-8, with Marauders at 0-2 and Technocrats at 8-10. I do think those ranges work, not least because people with low Banality ratings are pretty much insane and very easy for changelings to affect with magic. It's the Mists chart that's more of a problem.<br /> <br /> I've got round this by allowing mages to resist the effects of the Mists with Willpower, so that they can effectively skip a month-long coma and instead just 'sleep it off' when they go to bed for the evening.<br /> <br /> One thing I did leave off the list above is Legacies. I think the Legacy system is pretty one-dimensional and cartoonish - at least, for the Unseelie Legacies. It's hard to create a nuanced Unseelie character who isn't just 'eeeeeeeviiiiiiiiiil' using the Legacies from the RAW. The Nature and Demeanor system actually works better at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:49:38-07:00","id":609192,"title":"","content":"For the (hopefully) last time, Changeling 20th <i>will not</i> be a merger of <i>Dreaming</i> and <i>Lost</i>. The other 20th anniversary games didn't borrow or incorporate from nWoD. in fact the notion runs counter to the <i>point</i> of the 20th anniversary stuff. So can we please, please, PLEASE stop with the &quot;make it more like something else entirely&quot; arguments? If you want to play Changeling: the Lost, then go do that. Seriously, the game exists, it doesn't need to be invented again at the expense of Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Gah!<br /> <br /> As for kith diversity? here's what changeling has already...<br /> <br /> 15 Commoner Kithain kiths (16, if we count the Domovoye from the Boggan fanbook)<br /> 3 Noble Kithain Kiths<br /> 14 Nunnehi Families<br /> 4 Menehune families<br /> 8 Thallain Kiths<br /> 7 varieties of Adhene<br /> 6 Inanimae Phyla<br /> 6 Dauntain &quot;kiths.&quot; <br /> 10 Hsien Kwannon-jin<br /> <br /> There's also...<br /> <br /> 3 Mer noble Houses<br /> 13 Kithain noble houses<br /> <br /> The problem in Changeling is certainly not a lack of diversity. More like a lack of cohesion in that diversity. if you put a mer, a Fuath, two Boggans, and a glome together in a game, nothing is going to make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:58:01-07:00","id":609246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=609192#post609192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the (hopefully) last time, Changeling 20th <i>will not</i> be a merger of <i>Dreaming</i> and <i>Lost</i>. The other 20th anniversary games didn't borrow or incorporate from nWoD. in fact the notion runs counter to the <i>point</i> of the 20th anniversary stuff. So can we please, please, PLEASE stop with the &amp;quot;make it more like something else entirely&amp;quot; arguments? If you want to play Changeling: the Lost, then go do that. Seriously, the game exists, it doesn't need to be invented again at the expense of Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Gah!<br /> <br /> As for kith diversity? here's what changeling has already...<br /> <br /> 15 Commoner Kithain kiths (16, if we count the Domovoye from the Boggan fanbook)<br /> 3 Noble Kithain Kiths<br /> 14 Nunnehi Families<br /> 4 Menehune families<br /> 8 Thallain Kiths<br /> 7 varieties of Adhene<br /> 6 Inanimae Phyla<br /> 6 Dauntain &amp;quot;kiths.&amp;quot; <br /> 10 Hsien Kwannon-jin<br /> <br /> There's also...<br /> <br /> 3 Mer noble Houses<br /> 13 Kithain noble houses<br /> <br /> The problem in Changeling is certainly not a lack of diversity. More like a lack of cohesion in that diversity. if you put a mer, a Fuath, two Boggans, and a glome together in a game, nothing is going to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's the number of kiths that's been a problem for me. More how the basic premise of a splat (as a type of character class) is limiting for beings of the dreaming. Kiths with greater customisation as an optional rule would be perfect for me. Just something as simple as using Freebies to round out the fae mien and to buy Redes to create a more unique changeling. Merits and Flaws don't quite allow for the same flexibility. It would also shift the balance from cantrips to more individual talents during gameplay (which is good, because the cantrips are sometimes clunky).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:59:18-07:00","id":609354,"title":"","content":"I personaly think the Mists should have WAY less impact over other splats, or no impact whatsoever. They way they are now, its too easy for Changelings to isolate from others and too hard to interact with others. I do think it would be more interesting if even for a Changeling-only game the Fae had to actualy work to hide from other supernatural threats when they appear.<br /> <br /> About the Kiths, no one is talking about making The Dreaming equal to The Lost. It is just that, even keeping ONLY to The Dreaming, it would make a lot more sense to have more customisable characters. In fact, I don't think the list of kiths have to be greater, on the contrary, I think it is unnecessaryly huge! All that added, The Lost comes to mind just as an example of customization system. I could be talking about the rules for Race Creation on D&amp;D 5th Edition Dungeon Master Guide all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:20:04-07:00","id":609467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=609354#post609354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personaly think the Mists should have WAY less impact over other splats, or no impact whatsoever. They way they are now, its too easy for Changelings to isolate from others and too hard to interact with others. I do think it would be more interesting if even for a Changeling-only game the Fae had to actualy work to hide from other supernatural threats when they appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mists are way more punitive than the Delirium or the Fog, so I agree that there should be some options that allow inter-species interaction from time to time without everyone just forgetting the fae and turning into Sleeping Beauty. There are fudges that can be made, but my wiki of house rules over at RPoL has become gigantic :P<br /> <br /> However, having seen the text for Wr20's Spectres and Arcanoi chapters (or the excerpts that have been released anyway), I'm anticipating a very polished C20. So I do think most of these quibbles will be addressed. I see something like the smooth intuitiveness of Wr20, with a few toolkit options to allow for greater imagination <i>a la</i> M20 (but without quite so much bloat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:52:29-07:00","id":609619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=609246#post609246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's the number of kiths that's been a problem for me. More how the basic premise of a splat (as a type of character class) is limiting for beings of the dreaming. Kiths with greater customisation as an optional rule would be perfect for me. Just something as simple as using Freebies to round out the fae mien and to buy Redes to create a more unique changeling. Merits and Flaws don't quite allow for the same flexibility. It would also shift the balance from cantrips to more individual talents during gameplay (which is good, because the cantrips are sometimes clunky).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's actually a reason for this, mentioned time and time again in the changeling books. it <i>usedto be</i> that there were no &quot;kiths,&quot; just an infinite array of fae, godlings, Good Folk, and the like. However, the Shattering changed that. Arcadia closed up, and the flood of glamour it provided the Autumn World slowed to a trickle, while banality surged in the Autumn World. The fae who remained took on the Changeling Way - basically embracing Banality to some degree. This had the effect of &quot;regulating&quot; their Kiths. Similar sorts of fae basically grew together, as legends consolidated; the house-elf of a manor became the same as a field-harvesting spirit on the peasant's land, and they both became &quot;boggans.&quot; It wasn't a <i>fast</i> change; <i>Kithbook: Sluagh</i> mentioned the &quot;buttery Spirits&quot; who were an independent kith, but who apparently merged with the Sluagh as their myths became merged by mortals. Kithbooks Redcap, Satyr, and Troll all also mention kiths that became extinct in this time, but who they identify as being &quot;related.&quot; When the Sidhe came back to earth, it caused a new wellspring of glamour... but not so much that it actually forced banality back. To survive, they had to adopt mortal flesh as well, restraining themselves with banality just as the commoners did. <br /> <br /> Banality is the reason that the Kith exist as defined &quot;species&quot; of fae, rather than every changeling being a unique, wild assortment of potential like we see in Dark Ages; Fae.<br /> <br /> The system you're looking at is, in fact, easily replicated in merits and flaws. MET Changeling actually lets you take other Kith's Birthrights and frailties with a merit or flaw. And creating a merit that gives your character a Rede (at variable cost) seems easy enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:18:07-07:00","id":609822,"title":"","content":"My problem with the Gallian is that trying to to have a group that consists of Kithian, Inanimae and Adhene is such a freaking headache because they all use different mechanics as to how they work. A more universal system of mechanics so that they run a little more smoothly together would be appreciated. And I get that they all have different cultures and philosophies, nothing wrong with that, but do the Hsien <i><b>HAVE</b></i> to be such a pain in the ass to play with western Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:46:17-07:00","id":609897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=609619#post609619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system you're looking at is, in fact, easily replicated in merits and flaws. MET Changeling actually lets you take other Kith's Birthrights and frailties with a merit or flaw. And creating a merit that gives your character a Rede (at variable cost) seems easy enough to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking other Birthrights and Frailties, or Redes, as Merits and Flaws is actually the system I favour. So we're in agreement, I think. It's simple and doesn't require porting over CTL's rules (although I did like the idea that cropped up on these forums recently to allow characters to pick a kith from CTD and then a 'sub-kith' from CTL--but of course, that's not for everyone).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:35:36-07:00","id":610108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=609822#post609822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Gallian is that trying to to have a group that consists of Kithian, Inanimae and Adhene is such a freaking headache because they all use different mechanics as to how they work. A more universal system of mechanics so that they run a little more smoothly together would be appreciated. And I get that they all have different cultures and philosophies, nothing wrong with that, but do the Hsien <i><b>HAVE</b></i> to be such a pain in the ass to play with western Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur with this statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:48:36-07:00","id":610323,"title":"","content":"1.) GETTING RID OF SCIENCE = EVIL AND BANAL!!!!! <br /> <br /> 2.) Chemerical reality being less stupid<br /> <br /> 3.) changeling20 having a clear goal of what it wants to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:04:50-07:00","id":610364,"title":"","content":"Stopping to think about it, I don't think Science = Evil as being a good idea for the setting anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:30:18-07:00","id":611100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=610323#post610323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) GETTING RID OF SCIENCE = EVIL AND BANAL!!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>It never was. <i>Never</i>. There's an entire Kith focused on science - hell, there's even a Nunnehi Family that embraces technological advancement, in their way. What's banal is how these things are <i>used</i>. Television is a good example. Television is generally banal not because of some inhernet evil of cathode ray tubes (or plasma screens, I guess) but because it lends to people sitting on their butts staring at it all day, letting it think for them, pioping someone else's thoughts into their heads for an average of seven hours a day. <i>But</i> television is also the cause of the Resurgence, the biggest explosion of glamour since the dark ages, due to people captivated by the Moon Landing - itself a product of hard science.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, subsequent Apollo missions became &quot;boring&quot; - we knew we could do it, it had been done, and became banal. The moon went from a massive achievement, a great leap outward for mankind, and became a lifeless ball of dust where some nerds in doofy diaper-suits played golf. <br /> <br /> The use of science to &quot;reduce&quot; things is banal, but the use of science to <i>discover</i> things is not. Over-reliance on and total absorption in technoilogy is banal, but technologfy itself is not - technology is a method of solving problems and improving lives, and clearly needs inspiration to get going.<br /> <br /> It's a balancing act. A changeling who owns a smartphone is in no danger from banality. A changeling who spends all day playing candy crush on the thing and only communicating in grunts when spoken to, however, <i>is</i> in danger from banality.<br /> <br /> It's sort of like how <i>visiting</i> Disneyland is a fun vacation, but <i>working at</i> Disneyland is a soul-crushing nightmare.Disneyland is not inherently one or the other, it's the human experience and interaction with Disneyland that makes the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) Chemerical reality being less stupid </div> </div> </div>Chimerical reality is literally what you make of it. If it's &quot;stupid&quot; at your table, maybe talk to your ST about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3.) changeling20 having a clear goal of what it wants to be. </div> </div> </div>THIS, I totally agree with. The latter portion of Changeling's print life ended up looking a lot like &quot;werewolf with pointy ears.&quot; Massive war! Dark spirits coming from Dimension X! To arms, to fight the Thallain and save the universe from the Wyrm, er, uh, Fomorians!&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:46:13-07:00","id":611116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=611100#post611100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It never was. <i>Never</i>. There's an entire Kith focused on science - hell, there's even a Nunnehi Family that embraces technological advancement, in their way. What's banal is how these things are <i>used</i>. Television is a good example. Television is generally banal not because of some inhernet evil of cathode ray tubes (or plasma screens, I guess) but because it lends to people sitting on their butts staring at it all day, letting it think for them, pioping someone else's thoughts into their heads for an average of seven hours a day. <i>But</i> television is also the cause of the Resurgence, the biggest explosion of glamour since the dark ages, due to people captivated by the Moon Landing - itself a product of hard science.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, subsequent Apollo missions became &amp;quot;boring&amp;quot; - we knew we could do it, it had been done, and became banal. The moon went from a massive achievement, a great leap outward for mankind, and became a lifeless ball of dust where some nerds in doofy diaper-suits played golf. <br /> <br /> The use of science to &amp;quot;reduce&amp;quot; things is banal, but the use of science to <i>discover</i> things is not. Over-reliance on and total absorption in technoilogy is banal, but technologfy itself is not - technology is a method of solving problems and improving lives, and clearly needs inspiration to get going.<br /> <br /> It's a balancing act. A changeling who owns a smartphone is in no danger from banality. A changeling who spends all day playing candy crush on the thing and only communicating in grunts when spoken to, however, <i>is</i> in danger from banality.<br /> <br /> It's sort of like how <i>visiting</i> Disneyland is a fun vacation, but <i>working at</i> Disneyland is a soul-crushing nightmare.Disneyland is not inherently one or the other, it's the human experience and interaction with Disneyland that makes the difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Chimerical reality is literally what you make of it. If it's &amp;quot;stupid&amp;quot; at your table, maybe talk to your ST about it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> THIS, I totally agree with. The latter portion of Changeling's print life ended up looking a lot like &amp;quot;werewolf with pointy ears.&amp;quot; Massive war! Dark spirits coming from Dimension X! To arms, to fight the Thallain and save the universe from the Wyrm, er, uh, Fomorians!&amp;quot; etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS! Although I never minded the Final Nights stuff, I prefer a wider focus in the supplement treadmill. Heroism and quests are great, as is politics in a hidden magic world, as is the search for inspiration and creativity. <br /> <br /> But from the 'setting agnostic' default of the other 20th Anniversary books, I'm not worried, as I think this is what we'll get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:59:56-07:00","id":611325,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Science is Evil and Banal&quot; thing is in the books. Saying it &quot;never was&quot; is more, &quot;it never ways at our table because we ignored parts of the books for other parts of the books.&quot; I'm not saying you're wrong to have gone the direction you did, but the issue with science and technology in CtD directly relates to #3 in that post: CtD doesn't know what it wants to be. Sometimes it wants &quot;Science is Banal.&quot; and sometimes it wants, a more nuanced approached.<br /> <br /> However, even when the books are being more nuanced, science and technology are still singled out as being particularly more prone to Banality than other human activities. The ability to inspire creativity, and excitement, for most things is the default assessment which has to be bucked before it becomes Banal. In science, and technology, the ability to inspire is the exception to it being Banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:51:27-07:00","id":611388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=611325#post611325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Science is Evil and Banal&quot; thing is in the books.<br /> <br /> Saying it &quot;never was&quot; is more, &quot;it never ways at our table because we ignored parts of the books for other parts of the books.&quot; I'm not saying you're wrong to have gone the direction you did, but the issue with science and technology in CtD directly relates to #3 in that post: CtD doesn't know what it wants to be. Sometimes it wants &quot;Science is Banal.&quot; and sometimes it wants, a more nuanced approached.<br /> <br /> However, even when the books are being more nuanced, science and technology are still singled out as being particularly more prone to Banality than other human activities. The ability to inspire creativity, and excitement, for most things is the default assessment which has to be bucked before it becomes Banal. In science, and technology, the ability to inspire is the exception to it being Banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No, I assure you, it is <i>not</i> in the books. Not in 1st edition, not in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:24:12-07:00","id":611553,"title":"","content":"Oh, it sure is...<br /> <br /> But it wasn't just in CtD, it was all across the cWoD. Mage included.<br /> <br /> The thing is, there where two kinds of science in the cWoD. One is the symbol of modern society, and since the setting was hugely inspired by a view of modern society as decadent and hollowed, it WAS inherently evil. Is the science represented in early editions as the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Yet other was the science of books of fiction. The science of Julius Verne, Isaac Asimov and George Lucas. Sometimes it comes close to actual science, but the sense of wonder is more important, and a certain literary feel. It was &quot;science&quot; only as far as it used technological trappings, but all the sense behind it made it clear it was something different from that &quot;other&quot; science.<br /> <br /> Certainly things got more blurred than that, but not because science wheren't evil. What happened was that the setting evolved with time, the themes transformed, and things sometimes got confused. The very concept of science as evil was, in fact, diminishing with time. Guide to the Technocracy tried to make amends for this and start the path to integrate science in the setting along the &quot;good&quot; guys and find better sources for the maladies of the world. Maybe too late.<br /> <br /> Each and every line before Revised, though, followed this reasoning. Science is evil. It can be redeemed under some circunstances, mixed with magic, but by default it is evil. It is the main tool of the Wyrm, the main source of Banality, the weapon of the Men in Black, and even if it can be a source of some goodness, it is only to deceive the naive or be snatched by someone who can truly turn it to good mixing with magic. Without it, science will lead humanity to its doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:56:28-07:00","id":611620,"title":"","content":"If 'science is evil!&quot; is written into a mage book, then i guess that's mage. I'm 100% certain that it's nowhere in changeling, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T23:38:06-07:00","id":611938,"title":"","content":"To have Neil Gaiman making the preface","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T05:23:49-07:00","id":612095,"title":"","content":"I think that Changeling, when all it's said and done, isn't anti-science. Its standing on the matter it's vague, but that's something that can be said about all that has to do with Glamour/Banality.<br /> <br /> In some book (don't remember if the storyteller's or the player's manual), its stated that what Changelings can use to get Glamour it's relative, and that some can use scientific creativity as a source of Glamour.<br /> <br /> Also, it's hard to maintain that Changeling it's anti-science when Shide come back because of the Glamour surge that represented the landing on the moon...<br /> <br /> I think that, as long as science brings new dreams (that it's, new fiction), it's never Banal (in Changeling terms). But when science works only to grease &quot;the system&quot;, or do &quot;serious, adult, stuff&quot;, it's not specifically Glamorous (but don't have to be Banal either).<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the greatest myths of Changeling it's that modern things, like labs, offices or even schools are Banal. That's just false. Because the Basic (2ed) explicitly states that there's no such thing as a &quot;Banal place&quot;. Banality comes from people, never from places. The only exeption are the Nunnehi, but only for purposes of traveling to the Umbra.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2015, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T07:13:55-07:00","id":612199,"title":"","content":"The exception about the Nunnehi is because that isn't about Banality, but about the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> And if science isn't a banal thing by itself, no Technocrat should have high Banality.<br /> <br /> It surely is vague, and I'm not saying the game is exclusively written with that idea. But it is present, showing up here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:15:54-07:00","id":612488,"title":"","content":"Okay, we can all agree that science isn't banal. but honestly one of the biggest complaints I've heard is that growing up is. I'm curious as to whether or this is something that should be changed or revised. personally, now that i have gotten a little older i don't think that banality and age are one in the same. with age comes knowledge, discipline, focus, understanding of the way the world and universe works, skill and experiences. in other words, in many ways age can help you become a better artist. ageing its self is not and should not be considered banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:54:00-07:00","id":612517,"title":"","content":"Aging in itself isn't banal. No rule in Changeling enforces a gain of banality when you age (as far as I know). No, what rules enforce it's a higher banality for older starting characters. Because it's common for adults to be Banal.<br /> <br /> This it's the explanation:<br /> <br /> Precisely because when you age you're more attuned to the realities of the world, you lose the ability to live with fantasy.<br /> <br /> Even the most imaginative writer fantasies ain't as intense as the ones of the child that genuinely believes in Santa, to the point of even bothering to argue how improbable it's for a guy like Santa to exist (like if it was something that could, or has to, be explained). Or those of the child that it's genuinely scared of monsters.<br /> <br /> No, adults are too attuned to the wonders and horrors of the real world, and that's Banality. Banality it's when the real world can more than your imagination, or when you have to adapt that imagination to the limits of the real world. Or, better, the limits that society thinks that the real world has. The landing in the moon shattered those limits, allowing Fae to enter the world<br /> <br /> I, personally, think that's why Technocrats are (and have to be) Banal. They're actively enforcing one true reality, they're agents of the &quot;real world&quot;. Even Void Engineers are striving to make the universe as &quot;clean&quot; as possible. When Technocrats are over reality will be the only truth, and imagination will be just that, fantasies (preferably, fantasies about the real world, not that fantasy nonsense). In enforcing one world, despite the overwhelming evidence that they have about the existence of magick and other worlds, Technocrats are blinding everyone to other posibilities, bringing forth Banality with their Enligthened Will.<br /> <br /> Oh, And Technocracy isn't &quot;science&quot;. Enforcing one view of Reality over all others isn't science, even if that view happens to be healthy to objective science.<br /> Science it's about discovering truth. Technocracy it's a secret society that happens to have a lot of scientist in their ranks, but it's main purpose isn't to discover new things, but to expel from reality any truth that seems dangerous to objective science. I invite you all to read the countless flame wars that have been fought about that theme in the Mage subforum, and to leave the issue of banal Technocrats as a poor crossover ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:59:53-07:00","id":612521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=612488#post612488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, we can all agree that science isn't banal. but honestly one of the biggest complaints I've heard is that growing up is. I'm curious as to whether or this is something that should be changed or revised. personally, now that i have gotten a little older i don't think that banality and age are one in the same. with age comes knowledge, discipline, focus, understanding of the way the world and universe works, skill and experiences. in other words, in many ways age can help you become a better artist. ageing its self is not and should not be considered banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Growing up&quot; was probably intended to be used as shorthand for, in the words of Survivor, trading your passion for glory. You stop doing things because you enjoy them and start just going through the motions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:20:38-07:00","id":612640,"title":"","content":"About growing up, tough I do understand you point, <b>DeeDee</b>, I would at least partialy side with Aleph. But in the end it had to do with the vision the authors had at the time over the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> I can't agree with you here, <b>Aleph</b>. First of all, because it ignores the changes on the Technocracy over editions. They are more successful, but not more applied to the task of controlling the Consensus as any other Mage. They DO work to bring new wonders upon the world, even if they want to keep all the fun of the process to themselfs (with the implied danger). They don't want a Static reallity. Surely, what the Technocrats do isn't science, any more than the works of Etherites, Glass Walkers or Knockers. It is magic in the trappings of perceived &quot;science&quot;.<br /> <br /> Second, science is about discovering what is real and what isn't. It is wonderful, but also paves our understanding of reallity. The moon landing, by itself, isn't science, even if made possible by science. You say Banality is to stay attuned to the wonders and horrors of the real world instead of fantasy. If so, science is Banal by definition, plain out.<br /> <br /> What brings us again to the question of defining Glamour and Banality. Because I don't understand Banality in the same way, but that is a valid interpretation. And one that brings again the Science is Evil theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:37:11-07:00","id":612779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't agree with you here, <b>Aleph</b>. First of all, because it ignores the changes on the Technocracy over editions. They are more successful, but not more applied to the task of controlling the Consensus as any other Mage. </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>One World, One Truth, One Reality</i>&quot;. How it's that they aren't more driven to controlling the Consensus than any other mages?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't want a Static reality. </div> </div> </div>Bring statism to the world it's the 1rs principle of Damian. Principles of Damian weren't retconned, the last time I checked.<br /> <br /> While an individual technocrat might be more focused on other principles, bringing a Static Reality it's still one of the fundamental missions of the technocracy. You can interpret this in many ways, from discovering everything to controlling everything, but one thing that Technocracy DOES want it's a Static reality (which they interpret as one that isn't always changing to the whims of reality deviants, not as a frozen world, of course)<br /> <br /> And about science being paved on the real world. That's true, but to be a scientist you need to defy the preconceptions that build up that real world.<br /> <br /> Paving these preconceptions (faeries don't exist, monsters don't exist, you dad has cancer and it's going to die because miracles don't exist) it's Banal for sure (and should be so). Being skeptic it's Banal, paving the pragmatic &quot;real world&quot; of the adults it's Banal too, by extension.<br /> <br /> But it has been said, with reason, that being a scientist isn't about bringing forth skepticism. Each time a scientist breaks the barrier of what it's possible, or dreams of bringing an utopic world, it shouldn't be Banal, I think.<br /> <br /> The books aren't clear on the issue, and if a poorly written crossover with Mage it's all the proof on the contrary, I think those aspects of science that bring forth new dreams shouldn't be Banal. Even if science can bring Banality too, when it plays it's &quot;skeptic&quot; role. <hr /><br /> One thing that always bothered me about Glamour/Banality it's the fixed idea that these are opposite and can't coexist (exept in Changelings, that can have both a high ratting of Glamour and a high rating on Banality). I think that these two can coexist. A person can be very tied to the real world, and pour a lot of creativity in being so. If Glamour and Banality could coexist, then there would be no problem in a scientist being skeptic and creative at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-02-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T23:24:22-07:00","id":613046,"title":"","content":"One thing that I have to add, it's that despite what I have said about Technocracy in general, I think that giving Banality 8 as a minimum to Technocrats it's a<i> gross generalization</i>.<br /> <br /> While I think that, as an institution, Technocracy represents security and prosperity more than science and discovery. That's not to say that discovery and science aren't important within the Technocracy. Of course they are. Science may be secondary to protecting humanity, but it's there as a fundamental component of said protection.<br /> <br /> And I think that, as an institution, it's ok to make Technocracy Banal. Not only for the &quot;I don't believe in fairies&quot; shtick, but also because the Will of the Technocrats works towards a world where the faeries don't exist. I think that giving them a high Banality rating it's a good &quot;in game&quot; way to express how the Will of the technocrats affects Reality around them as agents of that everyday reality they work so hard to maintain (to the point of denying the masses impressive advances and discoveries, for a justified fear that they might be too much for them and cause a backlash).<br /> <br /> Even then, saying that all technocrats are Banal it's missing the point of technocrats as individuals. Individuals who may believe in utopia, and want to change things. Or that may want to study that reality deviant more than eliminating it's danger. Or that may spend more time discovering new cures than in deciding if these are too wierd for the Consensus. Said individuals are the ones that strive to push forward the Time table<br /> <br /> But I think that can be changed in a C20. That Banality table it's not core to the system.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Banality coexists with Glamour, there ain't no problem. An utopian technocrat might easily be a Banal hunter of fantasies, while dreaming of glamorous utopia. He will be a Glamour fountain, but toxic and dangerous to most Changelings (and he wouldn't want it other way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-03-2015, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T04:32:51-07:00","id":613217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=613046#post613046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I have to add, it's that despite what I have said about Technocracy in general, I think that giving Banality 8 as a minimum to Technocrats it's a<i> gross generalization</i>.<br /> <br /> While I think that, as an institution, Technocracy represents security and prosperity more than science and discovery. That's not to say that discovery and science aren't important within the Technocracy. Of course they are. Science may be secondary to protecting humanity, but it's there as a fundamental component of said protection.<br /> <br /> And I think that, as an institution, it's ok to make Technocracy Banal. Not only for the &quot;I don't believe in fairies&quot; shtick, but also because the Will of the Technocrats works towards a world where the faeries don't exist. I think that giving them a high Banality rating it's a good &quot;in game&quot; way to express how the Will of the technocrats affects Reality around them as agents of that everyday reality they work so hard to maintain (to the point of denying the masses impressive advances and discoveries, for a justified fear that they might be too much for them and cause a backlash).<br /> <br /> Even then, saying that all technocrats are Banal it's missing the point of technocrats as individuals. Individuals who may believe in utopia, and want to change things. Or that may want to study that reality deviant more than eliminating it's danger. Or that may spend more time discovering new cures than in deciding if these are too wierd for the Consensus. Said individuals are the ones that strive to push forward the Time table<br /> <br /> But I think that can be changed in a C20. That Banality table it's not core to the system.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Banality coexists with Glamour, there ain't no problem. An utopian technocrat might easily be a Banal hunter of fantasies, while dreaming of glamorous utopia. He will be a Glamour fountain, but toxic and dangerous to most Changelings (and he wouldn't want it other way).</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, rather than C20 including a table of suggested Banality ratings for all Tehnocrats, you'd rather they publish the individual Banality ratings of every single Technocrat in the universe? Let's be realistic. Yes, it's a gross generalisation, but we need a quick point of reference for what will usually be NPC antagonists in a game about faeries fighting back disbelief. The table doesn't claim Banality 8 is the minimum, but rather the lower end of average. There are always exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-04-2015, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:37:28-07:00","id":613352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=613217#post613217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically, rather than C20 including a table of suggested Banality ratings for all Tehnocrats, you'd rather they publish the individual Banality ratings of every single Technocrat in the universe? Don't be silly here. Yes, it's a gross generalisation, but we need a quick point of reference for what will usually be NPC antagonists in a game about faeries fighting back disbelief. The table doesn't claim Banality 8 is the minimum, but rather the lower end of average. There are always exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it would be kind of weird, because only in actual crossover situations should the Technocracy ever be involved with Changeling. The Technocratic Union is another game's antagonist, and therefore not an important focus. Autumn People are more important to Changeling than a bizarre setup where advanced technology is really mmmmajiqckue*.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Four ms and a silent q!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:18:48-07:00","id":613379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=613352#post613352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it would be kind of weird, because only in actual crossover situations should the Technocracy ever be involved with Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a very important point. The Technocratic Union is the antagonist organization of Mage: The Ascension. It does not necessarily exist as such in Changeling: The Dreaming (although I would expect in the allies and antagonists section there to mention of humans who have tapped into glamour in order to perform magic, and some of them might use it for technological based or uncreative purposes).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:34:03-07:00","id":613388,"title":"","content":"Honestly at this point, with the announcement of Vampire 4th Edition, I'd honestly rather a new edition of Changeling than a &quot;20th Anniversary&quot; rehash. Give them a dynamic magic system directly interacting with and drawing from dreams, allow for a broader representation of kiths (i don't know why only the Greek dreams of lust survived amongst European dreams there of; or why only Yoruban dreams of wanderlust; etc), create a coherent idea of what the Unseelie vs Seelie dynamic represents AND STICK TO IT, stop presenting science as banal by default (with the moonlanding as an outlier), etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:48:17-07:00","id":613399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=613352#post613352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, it would be kind of weird, because only in actual crossover situations should the Technocracy ever be involved with Changeling. The Technocratic Union is another game's antagonist, and therefore not an important focus. Autumn People are more important to Changeling than a bizarre setup where advanced technology is really mmmmajiqckue*.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Four ms and a silent q!</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I second this point. We need far more information and discussion on how we want changeling's enemies to be portrayed. Not to mention we all seem to be of a<u><i><b> Consensus</b></i></u> (pun intended) as to science does not equal banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:31:12-07:00","id":613626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=612199#post612199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if science isn't a banal thing by itself, no Technocrat should have high Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it were banal, Glass Walkers would be ahead of standard werewolves. They're not.<br /> <br /> And further, what the technocracy does is not &quot;science.&quot; If science could accomplish the stuff the technocracy does... there wouldn't be any reason for the technocracy to exist. Theirs is a case of abusing the (reversed) adage that &quot;magic being indistinguishable from sufficiently advanced science.&quot; They're like Star trek. They do fantastic, scientifically impossible stuff, but they involve a console and talk about photons passing through the auxillary data continuum to create a warp harmonic barrier. The technocracy's involvement with science is that they use (variations of) the <i>modern consensus</i> as paradigm. You think the standard off-the-rack NWO censor knows the inner workings of his energy pistol? No, he's James Bond, and Q just gave him something and said &quot;it shoots stuff.&quot;<br /> <br /> The banality of the technocracy comes from their agenda and worldview. The technocracy wants to make the world &quot;safe&quot; for mankind. This safe world has no magic. No spirits (and no deep spirituality.) it has no cultural differences, it has nothing with would ever impede or harass humanity, or elevate some humans over others (the technocracy accepts its own &quot;elevation&quot; as needed to bring about human equality in the long run see...) And of course, the technocracy are the guiding, controlling hands of this future, shaping - ruling - the world they want to see. There is no space in this Brave New World for things like the fae - and <i>certainly</i> no place for the wonders and horrors of the Dreaming!<br /> <br /> After all, remember that only one Convention has any real knowledge of Dimensional Science... and Void Engineer agents who begin to see subdimensions as anything other than hostile, alien threats is re-assigned after receiving therapy!<br /> <br /> <i>That</i> is what makes the technocracy banal. not the tools they use or the jargon they spout. Back when they were the Craftmasons and such, with faith as the leading edge of hteir sword, they were <i>still as banal</i> - And as House Liam shows us, not becuase faith is banal, but because it's that desire for control, repression, and active efforts to cleave the dreaming away from the world.<br /> <br /> And yes, there is plenty of dissent among the technocracy (especially if one follows the Reckoning plot) reform movements to make the technocracy less stifling, more open to potential . But that's <i>Mage</i>. To Changeling, the technocracy are still &quot;The Hidden Ones,&quot; people pulling strings with magic to further banality by squeezing the Dreaming out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 08-03-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:36:32-07:00","id":613637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=613379#post613379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a very important point. The Technocratic Union is the antagonist organization of Mage: The Ascension. It does not necessarily exist as such in Changeling: The Dreaming (although I would expect in the allies and antagonists section there to mention of humans who have tapped into glamour in order to perform magic, and some of them might use it for technological based or uncreative purposes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeeeell, it kinda does. It's not &quot;The Technocracy,&quot; and the fae aren't particularly aware of the agency. But the Nobles book DOEs talk about how the Sidhe have picked up cues about &quot;The hidden Ones,&quot; magical agents of banality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:36:03-07:00","id":613727,"title":"","content":"Sure, there are enough parallels that if you want them to be one in the same, they can be, and sometimes an entity in one game line is the exact same as in another game line in the occasional crossover supplement. However, in the core books for all of the classic World of Darkness games, things are not assumed to be exactly the same across game lines.<br /> <br /> Talking about how changelings and the Technocracy might interact in a crossover game can be fun (and it's certainly dominated a few threads in here lately), but Changeling: The Dreaming should not assume crossover with Mage: The Ascension by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T09:22:44-07:00","id":615211,"title":"","content":"So what <i>other</i> things do we want to see in <i>Changeling 20</i>? There must be more?<br /> <br /> Expanding on the 'more non-US setting stuff', I'd like to see changeling cultures in Europe. Most of the changeling myths in CTD are European in origin, and yet, we get very little setting info about the Old World. I imagine the political set-up could vary quite a bit.<br /> <br /> I'd really like the Kickstarter to include stretch goals for the unfinished Kithbook series, too. I mean, they only needed to do one more, and we have the core kiths covered.<br /> <br /> I understand the old Book of Glamour drafts will now be obsolete/superceded by the revisions in this book, which is good, but maybe Keys to the Kingdom could be a stretch goal too? I dunno. I'm just thirsty, damn it, and I hate to think I'd miss out on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:40:10-07:00","id":615283,"title":"","content":"I think the setting it's very good. Rather than change things, I would enjoy if they take time to clarify them. To clarify Glamour and Banality, to explain better how to storytell in two worlds at once...etc. Changeling has a lot of vague stuff out there that needs to be clarified or explored, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:53:21-07:00","id":616036,"title":"","content":"Clarification, clarification, clarification. A lot of clarification.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to expand on non-US stuff, but this time, <b><i><u>please</u></i></b>, do some serious research first!<br /> <br /> And seriously, not just Europe. I don't want to see my country being again pictured as Amazon Forest with a Banana Republic from a series of the 60's attached to it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T01:02:52-07:00","id":619868,"title":"","content":"Okay, some stuff in specific...<br /> <br /> <b>Re-write the <s>Accordance War</s> Sidhe:</b> I was gonna be happy with just asking for the accordance War to be less &quot;black hats vs. white hats,&quot; owing to the plain fact that civil wars are messy affairs that don't really work like that. But as another thread on the forums is pointing out.. .the sidhe are really written as total crapsacks all over the place. it's like the 2nd edition trend of &quot;the man&quot; splats just got totally flanderized. The sidhe aren't just <i>arrogant</i> - they're <i>completely and totally undeservedly arrogant</i>. sure the other &quot;The Man&quot; splats in the earlier games are snots. But.. .the Ventrue get stuff done. The Silver Fangs REALLY ARE heroes. The Order of Hermes are the strongest and most diverse magical tradition. The sidhe? The Sidhe are just pretty. And <i>all three</i> of those &quot;The man&quot; splats got a decent revision that made them multidimensional, engaging characters. The sidhe, and the affairs around them, really need a good overhaul. Either that or the game really needs to be refitted into &quot;Commoner: the Resistance&quot; and just leave the Sidhe as &quot;Well, you <i>can</i> play them, but...&quot; splats.<br /> <br /> <b>Balance the Houses:</b> I know, I know, &quot;game balance&quot; is the perpetual bugbear of these discussions, but this time, it's completely reasonable. Compare House Eiluned; their boon(s) are that they get a free success on every cantrip ever, and an unstated boon that they can get around the Gwydion lie-sense. Their flaw is that they are compelled to engage in intrigue - which means that their &quot;flaw&quot; is that they get involved in the side-plots the storyteller set up for them anyway. House Liam? -1 difficulty to enchant mortals (which in 2nd edition <i>has no difficulty</i> is their boon, while their flaw is basically that nobody ever trusts them about anything ever, period, forever. House Gwydion's &quot;unstoppable kill monster&quot; flaw is neat, sure, but does it really line up against Fiona's &quot;don't afraid of nothin'&quot; flaw? And is there any way to actually make Leanhaun <i>playable</i>?<br /> <br /> <b>Expand the non-core Houses:</b> There's tons of stuff for the five &quot;Seelie Houses.&quot; A fair bit for Ailil and Scathach as well. But what about the rest? I definitely want to see more from House Aesin (speaking of fixing boons and flaws...) and beaumayn. Speaking of Leanhaun, how's their Master Plan coming? A full &quot;Houses&quot; chapter would be really nice, really, but that might have to be its own book, like &quot;Lore of the Clans&quot; or whatever...<br /> <br /> <b>The Arts and Realms are Slapdash:</b> A five-success roll with Ensnare deals as much damage as getting run over by a riot tank (15) - But five successes with Primal 4 deals five damage. Talecraft is legendary in how not-good it is. The Arts introduced in Denizens follow some entirely different system, but are still regarded as available arts for changelings. Speaking of which, do inanimae and Hsien need <i>totally different systems</i>? Needing Actor 5 to affect anyone who is any sort of opposition to you is silly. Do you split successes when using hte Scene realm or not? Is every Realm usable with every Art (they should be). Nature 5 vs. Primal 2, wut? On and on down the list.<br /> <br /> <b>Not Just the Sidhe:</b> Okay. I get that the kith are archetypal beings. And of course, &quot;you can make any character you want.&quot; But... there needs to be internal support for diversity. A troll sorcerer or a boggan buttkicker SHOULD be options. The splats don't need mechanical helpers for this stuff, but loosening the lacings a bit, exploring how the various kith operate in a <i>variety</i> of situations and endeavors is definitely needed. What are redcap matchmakers like? (&quot;NOW KISS!&quot;) How do Pooka nobles do their thing? (&quot;NOW KISS!&quot;). <br /> <br /> <b>The Eshu are dicks. Fix them:</b> I recently read through the Eshu book. And, I have to say as badly as the sidhe are portrayed, the Eshu are just completely insufferable on all levels. Yes, one expects a splatbook to promote that splat with &quot;we're the best, everyone else isn't&quot; but DAMN, the Eshu are complete and total mary sues. Their only flaw is that they are so flawless that other people get jealous. Their major failings? A few times when commoners (I almost typed &quot;other commoners&quot; but no, the Eshu see themsleves as nobles...) didn't heed the Eshu. Yup, the failings of the eshu are completely the fault of their &quot;Lessers.&quot; And of course the Sidhe are portrayed as the crappiest crapsacks ever. Seriously, the Eshu come off as having major, major compensation issues (and looking at their kith-specific art, I almost can't blame them.) But if you don't use their Kithbook... there's really not much to them, they're the &quot;dudes who wander around&quot; splat, which is rarely compelling. Their frailty is interesting, but their Birthrights are both garbage... A power of being where the ST was going ot send you anyway, and a second one where you get a little more experience? Not engaging stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimera PC rules:</b> Please please please please.<br /> <br /> <b>Outlines for Historical settings:</b> The day before the Resurgence, what was the Turtle Empire like? How did the fae handle the High Renaissance? Will there be Dark Ages support? <br /> <br /> <b>Speaking of Dark Ages...:</b> Okay. I've waggled my finger earlier in the thread about &quot;if you want to play a different changeling game, play that different changeling game&quot; ...but... Dark Ages: Fae does have lots of stuff that could be pulled in in <i>some</i> fashion, even if only for fluff or inspiration for Arts or something along those lines. Fine, the Kith don't come in infinite varieties, that's fine, but does the Seasonal court system still have some unrecognized pull in the modern day? Are there actual True Fae extending their weird hands out and tugging things in the world? Are there still Gold Oaths binding fae and humanity that have been forgotten in the mists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:33:26-07:00","id":621337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=619868#post619868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, some stuff in specific...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=619868#post619868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Arts and Realms are Slapdash:</b> A five-success roll with Ensnare deals as much damage as getting run over by a riot tank (15) - But five successes with Primal 4 deals five damage. Talecraft is legendary in how not-good it is. The Arts introduced in Denizens follow some entirely different system, but are still regarded as available arts for changelings. Speaking of which, do inanimae and Hsien need <i>totally different systems</i>? Needing Actor 5 to affect anyone who is any sort of opposition to you is silly. Do you split successes when using hte Scene realm or not? Is every Realm usable with every Art (they should be). Nature 5 vs. Primal 2, wut? On and on down the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reworked all the Realms here: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/realms\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/realms</a>.<br /> <br /> And went over the Arts to describe how they might work with each and every Realm (such as using Captive Heart with Prop) here: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/Changes%20to%20Arts\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/Changes%20to%20Arts</a>.<br /> <br /> In general, damage needs fixing with Arts--it should be consistent. Even something as simple as the base damage dice pool being equivalent to the level of Art used, plus any additional successes on the casting roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/607021-changeling-the-dreaming-20-wish?p=619868#post619868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chimera PC rules:</b> Please please please please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I submitted some suggestions to OPP. In short, I'd use the Bygone Bestiary rules with a few tweaks: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/Character%20Creation%20for%20Changelings\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpol.net/?id=63447/Chara...%20Changelings</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T02:57:11-07:00","id":623198,"title":"","content":"Personally I would like to see a slip cover/case as a stretch goal that has the original spine art wrapped around, or on half of it.<br /> Otherwise seeing a rebalancing of Arts and Houses would be nice. I had no other issues with the second addition as the game set my imagination free and gave me the tools to play it my way! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1697-lostkith","name":"Lostkith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T10:11:28-07:00","id":625669,"title":"","content":"I also think it's essential that the errata, etc, collated here is incorporated: <a href=\"http://shadownessence.se/forum/topic/36246-20th-anniversary-edition-of-changeling-2nd-edition-feedback/\" target=\"_blank\">http://shadownessence.se/forum/topic...tion-feedback/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T15:45:39-07:00","id":630309,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would instead like to see DA: Fae ported in the modern era which I hope OynxPath considers this sometime in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:36:28-07:00","id":630720,"title":"","content":"Clarify banality and glamour. Give clarity on travel into and out of the Dreaming and its various layers. Some KIths are treated as universal archtypes AND Particular cultural things I'd like to see this clarified(Sidhe and Pooka are the most glaring here)<br /> <br /> Fix the hsien, even as someone who will defend KOTE I found the Hsien and odd choice, they don't share anything with Kithain whatsoever they'd make as much sense as random suppliment for mage or werewolf. They don't even make sense in setting as a replacement as they do nothing with the dreaming so one would assume that whatever lead to fae EVERY other place on earth would lead to them rising spontaniously in Asia and existing along side the little gods. <br /> <br /> Still part of the hsien thing but... Tanuki, a Pooka who picks a racoon dog as his animal form closer matches the myths and Japanese popcultural tropes of tanuki than tanuki. If I can't do <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Eccentric_Family\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Eccentric_Family</a> with a tanuki its a failed splat.<br /> <br /> Add some Hunters that don't come off as &quot;well meaning assholes&quot; banality shouldn't be the only threat to changelings.<br /> <br /> Do something with UFOs I mean its just sitting there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}